      "utf8": "the macro-to-micro to understand how to survive \nin this crumbling business, from the global  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96480,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "corporations all the way to three independents \nin the world's most competitive market."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109360,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We ignore phone calls, don't reply to texts, and \nleave emails unread. Spam hasn't slowed down. It's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "evolved and multiplied in the digital age. Modern \ntech didn't kill it. It supercharged it. AI,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119520,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "social media, and scrapers are now harvesting \nevery scrap of your digital life, all in the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123840,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "name of profit. And behind the scenes, there's a \nwhole industry making it happen - data brokers.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128480,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are companies who spend every waking moment \ncollecting your personal information, then selling  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132960,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it without your consent to marketers, scammers, \nand stalkers. Data brokers are making billions  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137600,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doing it and they're operating in the open. What's \nworse, even though they're legally required to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141840,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "delete your data if you ask, they bury that \nprocess in confusing legalese and endless hoops.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146800,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's all designed to wear you down. At Modern \nMBA, we're all tech-savvy. We've got blockers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151280,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "installed, rotate our passwords, follow best \npractices, and deleted our social media profiles  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156080,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "long ago. And yet, we were surprised when today's \nsponsor, Aura, uncovered over 30 data brokers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160800,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "still selling our personal information. They \ndon't own our data, yet they're making bank off  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164800,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it. That's robbery. With one click, Aura took care \nof the hardest part and removed our information  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169680,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from these websites. And most importantly, they're \ncontinuing to monitor to make sure our information  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174160,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stays off for good. Aura is an all-in-one digital \nsecurity that goes far beyond any tool you may  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179120,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "already have. Don't take a piecemeal approach to \ndigital security. Not having Aura is like locking  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183600,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the front door, but leaving your back door open. \nWith Aura, you get immediate alerts whenever your  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188160,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "info is found on the dark web, real-time fraud \nalerts for the one thing every hacker and scammer  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192480,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the world wants, which is your credit cards \nand banking accounts, and 24/7 monitoring on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197040,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "identity protection. On top of that, Aura has a \nbuilt-in VPN, antivirus, password manager, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202400,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more. Even if you've mastered your own protection, \nthe same can't be true for the other people in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206640,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your network. Scammers target the most vulnerable, \nand it only takes one weak link for things to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211360,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "go wrong. Aura protects you and your network. \nAura is not just watching from a distance. You  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215840,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get US-based support and fraud experts ready to \nhelp around the clock. Backed up to $5 million in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221440,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "identity theft insurance. It's one app with every \nlayer of protection. Try Aura free for 14 days at  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227200,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aura.com/MBA. In just these two weeks, you'll \ndiscover where your data is being exposed and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232800,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sold. We're not leaving ourselves vulnerable \nat Modern MBA, and you shouldn't either."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240800,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every industry has its gold rush. For cannabis, \nthe Green Rush started in 2012 when Colorado and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246880,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Washington became the first US states to legalize \nrecreational marijuana. The federal government's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252480,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hands-off approach signaled a seismic shift. \nPresidents from both parties began pardoning  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257040,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "marijuana offenses, backing decriminalization, \nand focusing enforcement on harder drugs. By 2023,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263520,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cannabis was legal for medical use in \n39 states and recreational use in 24,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268160,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it remains federally illegal, classified \nas a Schedule 1 drug, and banned from research.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273840,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This legal limbo blocks cannabis companies from \nbanking, tax deductions, and interstate commerce,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279200,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "essentials for any modern business. Still, \nlegalization was expected to drive explosive  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284800,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "growth. Investors and operators rushed in, betting \nthat weed could replace beer and cigarettes as the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290800,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "next billion dollar vice. The black market had \nlong dominated, but legalization reset the field,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296720,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "opening the door for someone to build the next \nMarlboro, Bud Light, or CVS for cannabis. As  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302720,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more states and countries joined in after 2012, \nevery link in the value chain, from farming to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307680,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "retail was up for grabs. Startups burned through \nmillions in venture capital and private equity,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313040,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "building fast and talking big. When Canada \nlegalized marijuana in 2018, it gave these  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318480,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "same companies the means to pump and dump. No \ncompany symbolized the hype more than Tilray, the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323920,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "first cannabis company to ever go public on a US \nstock exchange. By 2019, Tilray was the exclusive  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330080,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "supplier of medicinal marijuana to Novartis, the \nlead partner with Anheiser Busch on THC drinks and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335520,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the CBD distributor for authentic brands. But \nit was founded by VCs who boasted repeatedly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341360,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that federal legalization was coming soon and that \nlegal weed would disrupt Big Pharma, Big Tobacco,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347040,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Big Alcohol. Tilray stock soared from $30 \nto $180 in two months, hitting a $17 billion  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354400,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "valuation, 600 times revenue. Insiders quickly \ncashed out, but the international medicinal  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361520,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "business was all hype and no substance. Overseas \ncustomers were only accessible through tightly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366880,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "regulated channels with strict dosages and state \ncontrolled pricing. The real money was in the US,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 372480,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but as a NASDAQ listed company, Tilray couldn't \nsell there. That left Canada as the only option.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378320,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tilray tried to buy their way to dominance, \nacquiring smaller brands to enter higher margin  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 382880,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "edibles, vapes, and hemp alongside pharmacies and \ndispensaries. They merged with Aphria, Canada's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389360,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "second largest cultivator to create the world's \nlargest, lowest cost cannabis producer. The plan  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394560,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was to unify in exchange for majority market share \nin Canada and to wait out US legalization. Yet,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400560,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gross margins fell, showing that even the best \nfunded first mover couldn't avoid commoditization."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409680,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "5 years later after the merger, Tilray \nis still unprofitable and holds just 13%  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414560,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "market share in Canada. Even \nwith its economies of scale,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420160,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the company today earns more \nselling beer than selling cannabis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430720,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "MedMen rose to fame as the Apple store \nof weed, opening flashy dispensaries  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435360,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in upscale areas across every legal \nstate. But the company burned millions,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440000,
    "dDurationMs": 8720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "falsely believing traditional retail \neconomics didn't apply to cannabis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448720,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even as stimulus checks boosted sales for every \nretailer from Target to Louis Vuitton during the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453680,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pandemic, MedMen sales declined. Fancy storefronts \nweren't enough to build loyalty. In six years,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460560,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "MedMen fell from a $3 billion unicorn to \nbankruptcy. Even later entrance who tried  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466480,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to learn from these mistakes have struggled. \nBacked with $2.4 billion from big tobacco,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472080,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cronos tried to carve out a high-end niche. \nThey spent over $100 million over eight years  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477520,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on R\u0026D for stainless steel vapes, CBD skincare, \ngourmet edibles, and luxury infused body products  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484320,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "under the belief that brand power and product \ninnovation could be a moat. Despite owning  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 489760,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Canada's top selling brand in flower and edibles, \nCronos loses hundreds of millions of dollars  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 494880,
    "dDurationMs": 9520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "annually. Curaleaf, with 150 US dispensaries, is \nthe world's largest cannabis company by revenue.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504960,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But their scale and vertical integration \nwas all built on debt. Debt fuels growth  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510560,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but magnifies losses when revenue stalls. \nWith profits swallowed by interest,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515200,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Curaleaf also loses money to the tune of tens \nof millions of dollars. Trulieve chased emerging  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521920,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "states flooding Florida with hundreds of stores \nand a thousand different SKUs of flower, drinks,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526880,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and edibles. But because cannabis companies \ncan't move inventory across state lines, all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 532160,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that product can only be sold through their own \ndispensaries or wholesale to competitors who are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536640,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "already promoting their own. Even though Canada \nand the US are the top markets, the gap is huge.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542640,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Trulieve grosses four times more selling medicinal \nmarijuana in Florida alone than Tilray does in all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548640,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Canada. But they hold just 35% market share \nin Florida, and sales have dropped yearly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 559920,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even Green Thumb, the only profitable \npublic cannabis retailer and manufacturer,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564480,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has seen their growth slow and margins dwindle \nunder commoditization. Since no one knows if or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570960,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when federal legalization will ever materialize, \nthe big corporations can only focus on form factor  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576640,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as their only avenue for growth. Rather than \npersuading consumers to smoke or eat cannabis,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582080,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the focus has shifted to getting them to drink \nit. Whoever can make that canned hit brand they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586880,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all say will unlock billions more in sales. But \nthis feels like wishful thinking as branding has  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592160,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not proven to be a profitable moat for anyone. \nThere's a pattern. These corporations peaked  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597440,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "during the 2010s when they were the only game \nin town. Now with competition everywhere,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602320,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "profits have collapsed and no one has been able \nto figure out how to compete at scale on anything  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607040,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "besides price. From one angle, this was just a \ncase of too much supply for too little demand.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 613360,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "From another angle, commoditization was \nalways inevitable, but market correction  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618080,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shouldn't mean collapse. Alcohol and tobacco \nare like cannabis. They're also commodities  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623040,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with comparable regulations. If Anheiser \nBusch, Altria, and Philip Morris can all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 628400,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "carve out multi-billion dollar positions and \nmassive premium margins in alcohol and tobacco,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633360,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why hasn't the same happened in cannabis? It's \nclear that there's more dynamics at play than what  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 639040,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can ascertain from big company financials. The \nGreen Rush is over. What's left is just business.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 645840,
    "dDurationMs": 10960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Regulated, fragmented, ruthless, and perfectly \ncompetitive, where only the smartest survive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 656800,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Out in Central LA is Noelle, owner of Mecca \nMid City. Mecca has been around since 2012,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662880,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "6 years before California legalized recreational \nmarijuana and the competition flooded in.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668480,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Today she and her team are prepping the store for \n420, the biggest sales day of the year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 690000,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Noelle's been in cannabis since the 2000s. She was a real estate broker who broke bad, growing weed in her garage and slinging it on the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 697840,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "streets. After a few close calls, Noelle walked away \nfrom the black market and went legit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780739,
    "dDurationMs": 2941,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Noelle's lived through it all before legalization,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 783680,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through the Green Rush, and now the downturn. \nThe promise of easy riches during the Green  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788320,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Rush meant California got saturated with too \nmany cultivators, processors, manufacturers, "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 793680,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and dispensaries. Wholesale prices \nhave plummeted 70% in the past 4 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804000,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Retail prices by extension have declined. An \neighth of an ounce or 3.5 gram is the most  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809680,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "common quantity in which cannabis is sold. It's \nthe industry equivalent of a medium-size soda.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 815200,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The average retail cost of an eighth has dropped \n42% with comparable drops across edibles, vapes,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 821120,
    "dDurationMs": 7760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and pre-rolls in the state. Legal sales \nhave fallen for the second year in a row."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832560,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tax revenue from cannabis has dropped to its \nlowest since the legalization of recreational  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 837120,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "marijuana in 2018. This free-fall is also \nhappening in Colorado, Oklahoma, Oregon,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 843840,
    "dDurationMs": 1911,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Washington state. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 892871,
    "dDurationMs": 1993,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Noelle isn't losing sleep over the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 894864,
    "dDurationMs": 4256,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "corporations or dispensaries down the street. \nIt's not that people are losing their taste  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 899120,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for cannabis. It's that they're turning to the \nblack market, whose prices she can't match. Weed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 904400,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the black market today is at least 35% cheaper \nwithout taxes. In LA, the state excise tax is 15%,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 911840,
    "dDurationMs": 8240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sales tax is 9.75% and the city tax is 10% for a \ntotal of 35%. Customers pay this tax whenever they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920080,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "buy weed from Mecca or any other legal dispensary \nin LA. And instead of applying these taxes as one  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925600,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "combined line item to the purchase price, these \ntaxes actually compound, each one taxed on top  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930480,
    "dDurationMs": 8880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the last. The average retail price today for an \neighth is $23. for an edible is $13. Pre-roll is $18  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939360,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a vape cartridge $25. When purchased legally, \nthat's $8 more on the eighth, $5 more on the edible,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 947040,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "$6 more on the pre-roll, and $9 more for the \nvape. But when customers buy on the black market,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 952720,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they avoid these taxes entirely. To offset the \ntax revenue that's been lost to the black market,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 959200,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the state government has opted to raise the \ntax rate even further, which ironically will  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 963680,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only drive even more customers underground. The \ntotal tax on legal cannabis will increase to 39%  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970000,
    "dDurationMs": 1947,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in July of 2025. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 997709,
    "dDurationMs": 1559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's merit to the argument"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 999268,
    "dDurationMs": 7532,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the way cannabis is taxed in California is unprecedented. In the world of alcohol and tobacco, taxes are shared by multiple  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1006800,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entities through the supply chain. Excise tax on \nbeer and wine is paid by manufacturers as a fixed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1012400,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fee per gallon. Excise tax on cigarettes is paid \nby wholesalers as a fixed fee per stick. But in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1018880,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cannabis, the excise tax is a percentage that's \nplaced exclusively on the retailers rather than  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024080,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the manufacturers or wholesalers. But there's \na counterargument that it doesn't matter where  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1028880,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the excise tax gets imposed in the supply chain. \nCigarettes are the most expensive in the states of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1034240,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "New York, Rhode Island, and Connecticut. And the \nsame is true for spirits in Washington, Utah, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1040400,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oregon. The higher excise taxes in those states \nare imposed on wholesalers and distributors yet  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1045840,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it all gets thrown onto the customer. The only \nother legal drug where retailers are responsible  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1051200,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for excise tax is the e-cigarettes, but that \nrate is only 12.5% compared to cannabis's 19%.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058400,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "E-cigarettes are also taxed as a percentage of the \nlower wholesale or manufacturer price. Weed is not  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1064560,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only broadly taxed at a higher rate, but also \nat the highest amount at the retail list price.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1069600,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "California, Washington, Montana, and Virginia have \nthe heaviest excise taxes in the industry with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1075040,
    "dDurationMs": 8080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "19-37% on retail sales. California takes it \na step further than its peers. The 19% excise  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1083120,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tax is applied on gross retail sales rather than \nnet sales. This means that retail operators like  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1088560,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Noel get taxed on the total transaction amount \nper order before accounting for discounts or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1093680,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "returns. This is why most dispensaries operate \non a final sale basis - no refunds, returns, or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1100000,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exchanges. If they accept a return, they get hit \ntwice, once with the total loss on the product,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1105680,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and two with having to dig out of pocket to \npay the 19% tax from the initial purchase.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1111200,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But beyond high taxation and illicit undercutting, \nthe challenges for retailers nowadays is product.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1117440,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's out there is what you get, and the \ndays where you could just put any weed on a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1120960,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shelf and expect it to sell are long gone. Noelle \nhas survived by building her own supply chain.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1126880,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So while Mecca is the storefront, she also \nruns Signal, a cultivator, manufacturer,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1131680,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and distributor. Vertical integration enables Noel \nto produce exactly what she sees customers looking  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1137360,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for in store. The reason behind Mecca's longevity \nin her book is treating the product and space  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1142960,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with the service and attention of a neighborhood \nspecialty rather than a lowest bidder commodity  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1147760,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the industry has become. In a time where \ntrust is low and everyone is in survival mode,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1153280,
    "dDurationMs": 3459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "she's become even more cautious about what's going \non shelves.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1190000,
    "dDurationMs": 3718,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "18th century botanists classified weed into two categories,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1193718,
    "dDurationMs": 5642,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sativas and indicas, based on their differences \nin plant appearance and psychological effects.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1199360,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sativas stimulate mood and energy, making \nthem well suited for daytime and social use,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1204240,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while indacas offer seditive effects that are \nideal for sleep and pain. Over the centuries,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1209600,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "growers started cross-breeding sativas and \nindicas to create new hybrid strains. These  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1214800,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hybrids combined traits from both categories to \ndeliver more precise effects and were genetically  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1219920,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "optimized for larger yields and faster growth. \nThese days, hybrids dominate and customers care  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1226240,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "less about if their weed is a pure sativa or pure \nindica and they focus far more on how it makes  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1231280,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "them feel. Today, there are over 700 different \nstrains of cannabis, most of which are hybrids.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1237840,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every strain of cannabis gets branded with a \ncrazy name like donkey butter, cheetah piss,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1242320,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and apple fritter. Breeders do it to differentiate \ntheir seeds to growers. Growers maintain these  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1247680,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "names as a way to differentiate their harvests \nto distributors and retailers. And finally, the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1252400,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dispensaries keep these names as a way to spark \ncustomer interest and to set their inventory apart  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1257520,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the competition. That way, when customers \nfind a strain that they like, they'll ask for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1261840,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it by name. In 2022, Gelato and Wedding Cake were \nthe two bestselling flower strains in the state.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1268560,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A year later, consumers had shifted to Blue Dream \nand Biscotti. If you stock only the best sellers,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1274640,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you jump head first into a price war, pedalling \nthe same handful as everyone else. You stock too  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1279760,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "many exotics and you lose mass market appeal. \nChoosing strains is one thing. Ensuring quality  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1285120,
    "dDurationMs": 922,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is another. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1334950,
    "dDurationMs": 2810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For Noelle, it's less about names and more about the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1337760,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quality of harvest. Growing conditions in soil, \nhumidity, and season impact quality. These days,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1344000,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the few farms left are focused on pushing volume \nto survive, and even the harvest quality of one  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1348800,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "strain can vary wildly across farms. Some growers \nwill even proactively rebrand old strains with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1354880,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "flashier new names just to stand out more to \nbuyers and retailers like Noelle. Noelle's perspective  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1360880,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that without this hands-on QA and direct \ncultivation experience, corporations like MedMen,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1366240,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who try to make money by just opening as many \ndispensaries as possible, will always lose. If  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1371600,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you don't know what you're looking at, you'll get \nfooled by distributors or growers who are just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1375920,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "looking to squeeze newbies with subpar batches, \nfalsely labeled strains, and overpriced products.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1529520,
    "dDurationMs": 5072,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Noelle inspects shipments weekly, stamping the Mecca brand on flower that meets her standards. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1544023,
    "dDurationMs": 2646,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "She sources from her own growers and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1546669,
    "dDurationMs": 5411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "longtime local farms. In a market overwhelmed \nby outrageous strain names and fleeting quality,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1552080,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Noelle's strategy is to make Mecca a mark of trust, \na constant that other dispensary owners can rely  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1557680,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on regardless of changes in strain or supply. But \nin today's market, it's all about value. Despite  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1564480,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all the ambiance and curation, Noel isn't blind. \nThe black market is about to be 40% cheaper,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1570320,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and no retailer has ever survived exclusively \nselling high-end weed. And since she can't get  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1575680,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "weed any cheaper from the growers and wholesalers, \nshe's opted to grow it herself. The Mecca brand is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1581360,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "designed to compete on quality for price rather \nthan quality absolute. The average retail price  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1586720,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of an eighth is 20% cheaper than that of the \nbig-name brands, and it's a bargain that few,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1591760,
    "dDurationMs": 3050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if any, can match in this new race to the bottom. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1637851,
    "dDurationMs": 6629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "4/20 is the biggest day in the industry and the main event of the year for Noelle. Every year at Mecca, it's a different theme  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1644480,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and no costume or prop is ever reused. This \nyear's theme is Weedle Juice, her own spin on  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1650320,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Tim Burton classic. For past 420s, it was \nKill Bill, Super Mario, Alice in Wonderland,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1656560,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Great Gatsby. It's this local spirit that has \nallowed Mecca to take root in the neighborhood  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1661600,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well before corporate stores moved in. The event \nis as much a celebration for the loyal regulars  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1667440,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as it is a defensive shield against any other \ndispensary looking to challenge their market  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1671840,
    "dDurationMs": 1418,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "share in this area. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1693675,
    "dDurationMs": 2165,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "4/20 is one day on the calendar,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1695840,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but Noelle runs her event for two consecutive days. \nOn a normal day, Mecca grosses on average $22,000  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1703040,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in sales. On this 4/20, sales clocked in at $74,000 \nper day, over triple the regular volume. Given  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1710160,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the time and money invested, there's no reason \nto rush a teardown. And running the event a day  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1714720,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "longer captures customers that missed out on the \nday before. Mecca grossed $12 million during the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1721280,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pandemic, but annual sales are down to 8 million \nwith Signal averaging another $1.1 million a year.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1728560,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Both businesses run at a 25% operating margin. \nNoel's success is rooted in hyper local knowledge,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1735120,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and she's pivoting to wholesale to make up for \nlost retail income. Her next store is in Bell  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1740480,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Gardens in a rare green zone where surrounding \ncities have banned cannabis, which would make  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1744640,
    "dDurationMs": 2447,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mecca one of the first legal dispensaries.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1782560,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every day, rain or shine, 71-year-old Jay drives \nto ERBA's four stores to make sure everything's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1787920,
    "dDurationMs": 981,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "running smoothly. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1795852,
    "dDurationMs": 4068,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But he knows that once the 420 rush is over, the industry will slip back  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1799920,
    "dDurationMs": 3222,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into the slump it's been in for the last 3 years. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1826869,
    "dDurationMs": 3051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Growers have certainly been hit the hardest. Over  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1829920,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "7,500 have gone out of business in the past 5 \nyears, leaving just 4,000 licensed cultivators  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1835520,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the state. In percentages, that means that \nover 6 out of every 10 growers have gone out of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1840480,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "business. What happens upstream flows downstream. \n1 out of every 2 distributors and nearly 4  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1846080,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out of every 10 dispensaries have shut down. These \nnumbers only capture the companies that tried  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1851040,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to play by the rules. And it's plausible that \nsome of these exits are not true insolvencies,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1855840,
    "dDurationMs": 3192,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but a return back to doing business in \nthe black market. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1930910,
    "dDurationMs": 1330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a Brooklyn native,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1932240,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Jay's a straight shooter. To him, cannabis \nis just like every other business. And the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1936800,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "industry is suffering from both the practitioners \nand policy makers who fail to treat it like one.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1942400,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's happening today is as much the result of \nself-sabotage as it is poor governance. For Jay,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1948080,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the most important qualifications are common \nsense, discipline, and old school elbow grease -"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1953200,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "basic elements that the cannabis corporations \nand their VCs lacked. These intangibles are what  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1958400,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he believes has kept on top and would keep any \nbusiness in any sector alive through a downturn.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2082138,
    "dDurationMs": 2422,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While Noelle runs Mecca like a traditional  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2084560,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "retailer where every product is meticulously \nvetted as an extension of the store, Jay does  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2089680,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the exact opposite. ERBA in both name and design \nis a marketplace. Products are sold on consignment  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2095840,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and parts of the store are subleasased to \nbrands themselves. Urba isn't curating,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2100640,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's aggregating. Customers aren't told what to \nbuy. They're invited to discover it themselves.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2139804,
    "dDurationMs": 7076,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because ERBA runs on consignment, Jay doesn't buy any product upfront. His 1,200 SKUs eclipse that of Noel's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2146880,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and is closer to the scale of a Trader Joe's. \nAt ERBA, brands supply their own product, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2152240,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they willingly give up upfront sales in exchange \nfor shelf space at his four dispensaries. There's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2157760,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no carrying cost or inventory risk for him, and \nboth sides only make money when something sells.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2163840,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As a result, ERBA is not as deeply involved \nin the same price war as other dispensaries.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2169040,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Jay's not ever worried about predicting the next \nhit strain, falling behind on quality control, or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2174320,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "needing to match the competition on BOGOs. Instead, \nhis responsibility is to bring in potential paying  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2180320,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "customers. And the rest is up to each and every \nbrand within ERBA to close the deal for themselves  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2185280,
    "dDurationMs": 2090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with whatever they've chosen to stock. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2227600,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it's not a walk in the park. Consignment is \nonly possible when the shelf space is perceived  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2232400,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as valuable. If ERBA starts slipping in audience \nor relevance, brands won't stick around. Thus,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2238080,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even though quality control, stock, selection, \nand pricing is largely out of his hands, Jay is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2243360,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "responsible for everything else. He creates the \nspace, supplies the labor, brings in the traffic,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2249360,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "grows, the brand, and enforces service standards. \nAnd it's on him to make sure that it's all going  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2254320,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up every day. He makes it a point to interact \nwith every single employee at each of his stores  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2259440,
    "dDurationMs": 3105,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he drives through the neighborhoods watching \nfor competition. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2331829,
    "dDurationMs": 7211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Before ERBA, Jay spent three decades running restaurants across LA. In his 20s, he worked in Asia for his family's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2339040,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "import export business. He's never touched weed, \nbut he knows numbers, he knows people, and he knows  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2344960,
    "dDurationMs": 1434,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how markets move. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2364521,
    "dDurationMs": 2679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To Jay,  the problem is not the existence of the black  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2367200,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "market. It's that the city has let them thrive \nwhile taxing the very few that are left playing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2371520,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the rules. In LA, legal cannabis has become the \nexception, not the norm. There are almost 10 times  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2378160,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as many illegal trap shops selling weed under the \ntable today than there are legal dispensaries in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2383520,
    "dDurationMs": 869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the city.    "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2420450,
    "dDurationMs": 5150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not that California or Los Angeles \nhas turned a blind eye towards illegal cannabis.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2425600,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even though street value has declined, the state \nhas confiscated progressively larger amounts year  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2430720,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after year. In 2024, the governor boasted that his \noffice had seized over half a billion dollars of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2436720,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "illegal cannabis with the vast majority of bus \noccurring in Los Angeles County. But all this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2442000,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "enforcement has been concentrated on the supply \nside. There's no questioning the effectiveness of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2446800,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the American military-industrial police complex \nwhen applied to kicking down doors, scoring  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2451920,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "headline busts, and throwing the nth drug dealer \nin jail. Yet, the war on drugs has demonstrated  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2457200,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "time and time again that cracking down on supply \nwithout ever addressing demand is ineffective. Cut  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2462720,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "off one head and another will take its place. \nThe reality is that taxation, regulation,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2468000,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and enforcement are not separate. They're all \nconnected as part of the same system. But taxation  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2473280,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has become the black market's greatest subsidy. \nThe more aggressive the tax, the more customers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2478160,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are forced underground. As pessimistic as Jay \nsounds, he's not given up. He's thrown himself  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2483440,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into civil service for the longevity of his \nbusiness and the greater industry, one council  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2488240,
    "dDurationMs": 1483,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meeting at a time. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2546858,
    "dDurationMs": 7142,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ERBA grosses $35 million a year across all four stores. Store  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2554000,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "level operating margins sit at 12% higher than \nconventional retailers like Target or Home Depot,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2559360,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but not as high as vertically integrated stores \nlike Mecca. Lower margins are natural with a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2564480,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consignment business model. You trade away \nprofits and pricing in exchange for better   "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2568720,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cash flow, minimal inventory risk, and greater \nproduct mix. In our past episode on sneakers,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2574320,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we covered Legacy, which netted operating margins \nof 16% with its consignment ccentric business,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2579760,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is comparable to Urba's 12%. The \nreality is that consignment is not entitled,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2584800,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but rather earned by an elite few operators. \nWholesale is a standard across industries as every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2590560,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "brand looks to secure volume and revenue upfront. \nGetting so many vendors to buy into consignment,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2596320,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially in an industry as fragmented, low \ntrust, and competitive as cannabis, is a feat  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2601360,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that requires both a steady hand and deep reserves \nof social and political capital. All of which Jay  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2607360,
    "dDurationMs": 1422,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "uniquely provides. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2666526,
    "dDurationMs": 2034,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bobby and Nick founded HERB,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2668560,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "LA's longest running independent cannabis delivery \nservice. The pair met in the 2000s, and when the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2674240,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "opportunity came to go legit, they bet on that \nfuture. Herb has outlasted the Silicon Valley  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2679760,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Uber for weed startups who all burned through \nmillions but couldn't survive the industry's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2683920,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "strict regulations. Unlike food delivery, cannabis \ndelivery is tightly regulated. Every driver is a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2690400,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "W2 employee, can only work for one dispensary and \nmust handel every order. There's no proprietary  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2696960,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "algorithms, cutting-edge AI, or legal loophole to \nscaling a delivery network in this industry. In  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2702720,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a market where everyone sells the same products, \nHerb has sustained by sticking to the basics of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2707760,
    "dDurationMs": 965,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "customer service. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2761600,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "11 years in, Bobby and Nick have kept their team \nsmall and hands-on. They still answer the phones,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2767120,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and when drivers are busy, they'll make deliveries \nthemselves.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2774755,
    "dDurationMs": 2525,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The model is asset light. HERB is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2777280,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "located in an inconspicuous neighborhood, but the \nlower operating costs come at the trade-off of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2782080,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "visibility, but since every dispensary also offers \ndelivery of their own, being lean only helps with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2787920,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "startup, not growth. The lower barriers to entry \nmeans it's faster and cheaper to get started.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2793280,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But at a macro level, it's much harder to get a \nseat at the table without a physical presence.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2798240,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In California, 66% of weed delivery services have \nshut down in the past 5 years. That's a failure  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2804640,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rate that's nearly three times higher than that \nof brick-and-mortar dispensaries. Herb's business is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2810160,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "built more on product markups than delivery fees. \nTo drive volume, there's minimum order sizes.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2815520,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Customers get free delivery when they spend $50 or \nmore. But without the face-to-face interactions of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2820800,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a retail storefront, Bobby and Nick need ways to \ncompensate for this missing Goodwill. All of which  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2826240,
    "dDurationMs": 4482,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reduce profits but have helped Herb stand both \nabove the crowd and the test of time. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2928080,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In theory, Herb could handle deliveries for other \ndispensaries, but most already run their own and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2933200,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are struggling to hold on to their shrinking \ncustomer base. In these times, every player is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2938240,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "focused on holding on to their slice of the pie. \nThere's a strong reluctance to share clientele  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2943120,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and little appetite for shotgun marriages. This \nis why there's little opportunity for Herb to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2948240,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "build its future in B2B, even though they have the \nsuperior network and logistics and Bobby, Nick,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2954960,
    "dDurationMs": 2885,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Noel, and Jay all share a common enemy. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3013621,
    "dDurationMs": 10459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "HERB grosses on average $250,000 a \nmonth for an annual run rate of $3 million."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3024080,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their operating margins sit at 5%, which is low \ncompared to the brick-and-mortar dispensaries. But  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3029760,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when you compare their margins to other on=demand \ndelivery companies like Uber as an apples to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3034480,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "apples comparison, HERB falls right in line,\neven with significantly higher payroll costs,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3039680,
    "dDurationMs": 2795,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "employing drivers as W-2 employees. "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3064459,
    "dDurationMs": 5861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Noelle, Jay, Bobby, and Nick are all part of a dying \nbreed of legal operators in LA who have each  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3070320,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "found ways to win in the most saturated \nmarket in the world. Noelle's edge lies in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3075360,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "product and vertical integration, which allows \nher to tailor her supply chain towards serving  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3080000,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this one specific neighborhood and to slowly \nexpand towards B2B from B2C. Jay's edge is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3086000,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in operations and relationships where his primary \ncustomers are brands and staff who all thrive off  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3091360,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "his political and social capital. Bobby and \nNick's edge lies in convenience and range.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3096800,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With a business that's shielded from real estate \nand foot traffic fluctuations, their respective  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3102080,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "expertise in LA is what's fueled their success \nover the corporations. These big companies just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3107120,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "don't have the means beyond mass advertising and \nfirst mover to win meaningful market share. This  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3112560,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is why every multi-state operator has effectively \nleft California in pursuit of easier, uncontested  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3118240,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "dollars elsewhere. Noel, Nick, Bobby, and Jay are \nall doing things that don't scale. Whether that's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3124560,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "running deliveries, picking out their own flower, \nor greeting every single employee, and they all do  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3130240,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this so they can spot trends faster, outmaneuver \nthe competition, and maintain a foothold in this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3135600,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one city in California. But ERBA, HERB, and Mecca \nare all outliers in the grand scheme of things.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3142080,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their solo wins at the micro level in this one \ncity are not enough to stem the bleeding across  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3146720,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the state and industry. The collapse of legal \ncannabis is a modern case study that proves  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3151440,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that America is just a business. It's a country \nwhere politics follow the economy and not the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3156800,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other way around. The industry's current state \nis more so a failure of policy than business.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3162480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Politicians saw legal cannabis as an infinite \nmoney glitch where this magical never-ending  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3167280,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tax revenue would fund these flashy headline \npublic projects that could propel them further  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3171920,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in their own careers. It had nothing to do \nwith the progressive populism, social justice,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3177040,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or medical advancements that they campaigned \non years ago to win votes as advocates of legal  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3181840,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cannabis. These politicians aren't interested \nin the long-term health of the industry,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3186160,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "only in the short-term collection of license fees \nand taxes to further their own self-interests.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3191760,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These politicians in this regard are ultimately \nno different than the venture capitalists that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3196400,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pumped and dumped weed stocks. But to return \nto business, the greatest skill is to make  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3201440,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something out of nothing. Noelle, Bobby, Nick, \nand Jay could have all exited or migrated to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3207440,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a less competitive state a long time ago. But in \nthe end, they're builders who are in it for the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3212560,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "long haul. They're still playing their cards, \nno matter how weak the hands are right now.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3216960,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not the venture capitalists or the corporate \nsuits, but instead these bootstrapped owners  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3221360,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who have the real business acumen that's \nworth learning from and are savvy, tough,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3225840,
    "dDurationMs": 7946,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and shrewd enough to turn a profit year after \nyear in this crazy crumbling industry. "
    } ]
  } ]
